WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Marcus applies for life insurance on himself, pays the premium and

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.020
names his sister Aisha as beneficiary.

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.520
Marcus is the insured because the contract covers his life.

4
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.260
He is also the policyowner, with the rights granted by the

5
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.320
contract, and the premium payer.

6
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.940
Aisha is the designated recipient of the death benefit under the

7
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.600
policy's terms. In another arrangement, these roles can belong to different

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.040
people. Always identify each role from the facts.

9
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.640
Paying a premium alone does not prove that the payer owns

10
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.680
the contract or controls its beneficiary designation.

11
00:00:36.738 --> 00:00:41.558
Maryland permits an individual with competent legal capacity to obtain

12
00:00:41.558 --> 00:00:44.998
coverage on that individual's own life for the benefit of any

13
00:00:44.998 --> 00:00:50.038
person. Marcus can therefore make a genuine own-life purchase and name

14
00:00:50.038 --> 00:00:55.198
the beneficiary he chooses, subject to the contract and applicable law.

15
00:00:55.878 --> 00:01:00.738
Do not confuse this with an unrelated investor causing a policy

16
00:01:00.738 --> 00:01:03.578
to be purchased on Marcus for the investor's benefit.

17
00:01:04.838 --> 00:01:06.158
The actual procurement matters.

18
00:01:06.978 --> 00:01:11.638
A signature used to disguise a stranger's scheme does not establish

19
00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:15.418
that the transaction was genuinely Marcus's own decision and purchase.

20
00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.580
Now Elena wants to obtain coverage on her spouse.

21
00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:25.540
Maryland recognizes a substantial interest based on love and affection

22
00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.720
for people closely related by blood or law.

23
00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.100
This is not a requirement that every spouse prove a specific

24
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.400
unpaid debt. Other relationships need their own analysis.

25
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:43.220
Friendship alone does not automatically establish the statutory family

26
00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.260
interest. The law also addresses prospective adoption with

27
00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.780
defined events and required conditions.

28
00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:55.760
Read the relationship carefully, then apply the appropriate rule.

29
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.120
A producer should not replace the legal test with assumptions about

30
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.780
a person's name, appearance or community.

31
00:02:03.798 --> 00:02:07.498
A small firm depends on Daniel's specialized work.

32
00:02:08.278 --> 00:02:13.258
His death would create a real economic loss through recruiting, training

33
00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:18.378
and interrupted operations. A lawful and substantial economic interest

34
00:02:18.378 --> 00:02:23.698
in his continued life can support an insurable interest, subject to

35
00:02:23.698 --> 00:02:29.018
the applicable requirements. Contrast an unrelated stranger who profits only

36
00:02:29.018 --> 00:02:34.158
if Daniel dies. An interest created only by death, or

37
00:02:34.158 --> 00:02:38.778
increased in value by death, is not the required economic interest.

38
00:02:39.618 --> 00:02:43.278
Insurance should protect a legitimate relationship or exposure.

39
00:02:44.298 --> 00:02:46.898
It should not create a wager on a stranger's death.

40
00:02:47.476 --> 00:02:52.356
For a person procuring coverage on another individual, Maryland's general

41
00:02:52.356 --> 00:02:56.256
rule permits the benefits to be payable to the insured, the

42
00:02:56.256 --> 00:03:01.116
insured's personal representative or a person with an insurable interest when

43
00:03:01.116 --> 00:03:02.356
the contract is made.

44
00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.716
Focus on that starting point.

45
00:03:05.656 --> 00:03:08.456
Do not move the test automatically to the claim date.

46
00:03:09.236 --> 00:03:14.496
Later ownership changes, assignments and beneficiary questions require

47
00:03:14.496 --> 00:03:19.716
their own rules. Likewise, a changed family relationship can

48
00:03:19.716 --> 00:03:21.596
raise separate legal issues.

49
00:03:22.436 --> 00:03:26.536
Establishing insurable interest when the policy begins is one question;

50
00:03:27.156 --> 00:03:30.096
determining who receives a later benefit is another.

51
00:03:30.886 --> 00:03:35.726
Insurable interest does not by itself answer every consent question.

52
00:03:36.586 --> 00:03:41.586
For an ordinary individual contract within Maryland's general rule, the

53
00:03:41.586 --> 00:03:46.106
insured must have competent legal capacity and apply for or consent

54
00:03:46.106 --> 00:03:47.506
in writing to the contract.

55
00:03:48.606 --> 00:03:53.126
The statute has specific exceptions involving spouses, minors,

56
00:03:53.986 --> 00:03:57.306
family policies and a person unable to consent.

57
00:03:58.646 --> 00:04:01.406
Group life is outside that subsection.

58
00:04:02.606 --> 00:04:07.366
Apply the actual exception rather than announcing that written consent is

59
00:04:07.366 --> 00:04:10.526
either always required or never required.

60
00:04:11.506 --> 00:04:16.586
Before submitting a file, confirm the roles, the interest, the

61
00:04:16.586 --> 00:04:20.706
required application and the insurer's documentation process.
